From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:02:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y: allow powering
 off the WLAN card

The WLAN part of the QCA9379 on SDHC2 is powered by L11, the vmmc
supply of SDHC2, and its reset line is GPIO 75 in wlan_pwrseq, so the
card can be fully switched off and back on. Two observations back this
up: unbinding and binding the SDHC2 host, which switches L11 off, brings
a hung card back; and the board's wlan_3v3 regulator (GPIO 77) is never
enabled, yet WLAN works. Bluetooth, the other half of the chip, does not
depend on L11: with ath10k_sdio not loaded or removed, the card runtime
suspended and L11 disabled, Bluetooth still sets up from scratch and
scans.

The card sometimes stops answering CMD52 when its driver probes ("timed
out while setting default block size", or later "Could not init hif"),
and then stays in that state across warm reboots, because nothing
removes its supply. On one unit this hit up to half of the boots.
Resetting it through wlan_pwrseq when the host probes does not help,
nor does one extra power cycle of the slot at that point.

The vendor kernel powers the card down right after enumeration and
powers it up again, with a full SDIO reinitialization, when the WLAN
driver registers. cap-power-off-card lets the MMC core do the same: it
runtime suspends the idle card after enumeration and powers it up with
a full reinitialization when ath10k_sdio probes. On the tested units
ath10k_sdio is loaded later from the root file system, so the card is
off for about 20-35 s at boot.

The I/O rail (L12) must remain on at 1.8 V while the card is off.
With that supply configuration and cap-power-off-card, each of two
units prone to boot or resume failures brought up Wi-Fi on all 30
warm reboots. The unit with timeouts previously failed 2 to 7 times
per 15 boots.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.2-astra
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/4a4328524ace516c3aa29c97f366e904dd411761
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
index 1905b780bd6a..ffaa60ba653e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -561,6 +561,7 @@ &sdhc_2 {
 	vqmmc-supply = <&pm8953_l12>;
 
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&wlan_pwrseq>;
+	cap-power-off-card;
 	non-removable;
 	wakeup-source;
 	/* Some devices experience dropouts of the WiFi module at the default of
